WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.671
A: Most pharmacies still run on fax machines, phone calls, paper logs, and systems that don't talk to each other.

00:05.671 --> 00:09.252
A: The lot, the patient, and the prescription live in three different places.

00:09.252 --> 00:15.222
A: Chimera Rx shows what a modern pharmacy system looks like: one connected ledger, from the dock to the pickup counter.

00:15.222 --> 00:16.714
A: Show them how that works.

00:16.774 --> 00:17.073
B: Sure.

00:17.073 --> 00:21.854
B: Staff sign in with a password and a six-digit code, and the server checks every role.

00:21.914 --> 00:24.301
B: Today shows each person only their own work.

00:24.361 --> 00:25.935
B: A technician receives a delivery.

00:25.935 --> 00:30.973
B: Scan the label, and the lot gate checks the paperwork, the expiry, and the recall list.

00:31.033 --> 00:39.097
B: The pharmacist sees stock by lot, with expiry and shelf location, then fills and verifies each order while Rx Watcher checks the rules.

00:39.157 --> 00:40.729
A: Least privilege is the point.

00:40.729 --> 00:44.186
A: The cashier runs the register and can't see allergies or recalls.

00:44.246 --> 00:47.406
A: Refills show who is due, and each patient keeps one history.

00:47.466 --> 00:49.204
A: Here's the gap old systems leave.

00:49.204 --> 00:53.839
A: A recall fax arrives, and nobody captured the lot, so you warn everyone, or no one.

00:53.899 --> 00:55.479
B: Connected, it takes seconds.

00:55.479 --> 01:02.983
B: The pharmacist confirms the lots, stock moves to quarantine, and the exact patients appear, with messages drafted for approval.

01:03.043 --> 01:04.871
A: Everything speaks open standards.

01:04.871 --> 01:08.983
A: DSCSA and EPCIS exports give every package a history.

01:09.043 --> 01:15.666
B: Here the sandbox verifier checks a package: a real serial verifies, and a spoofed one comes back not verified.

01:15.726 --> 01:21.179
B: Partners connect through a REST API, an MCP server, FHIR behind OAuth, and signed webhooks.

01:21.179 --> 01:25.178
B: The admin controls who gets in, and every call is audited.

01:25.238 --> 01:28.808
A: Two stores can transfer stock, and both audit logs record the move.

01:28.868 --> 01:38.670
A: The real-world connections, like text, email, phone, wholesaler, e-prescribing, the health record, payer, and single sign-on, are designed seams, sandboxed today, so nothing reaches a real person.

01:38.730 --> 01:39.925
A: Now the AI agents.

01:39.925 --> 01:47.993
A: Eight of them help in the background, and every one follows one rule: rules decide, the model explains, a gate checks the model, and a pharmacist decides.

01:47.993 --> 01:49.487
A: Take us through Rx Guardian.

01:49.547 --> 01:55.151
B: Rx Guardian works on its own, even when nobody is looking, and never changes an order itself.

01:55.151 --> 02:02.073
B: Run it now, and it flags things a busy pharmacist could miss, like duplicate therapy, an interaction, or a late fill.

02:02.133 --> 02:04.869
B: Each suggestion shows its evidence from the patient's history.

02:04.869 --> 02:08.516
B: Accept one, and the order goes on hold with the reason recorded.

02:08.516 --> 02:10.948
B: Dismiss it, and that reason is kept too.

02:11.008 --> 02:12.941
A: The Coroner gate is the safety net.

02:12.941 --> 02:17.913
A: It keeps only lots printed word for word on the recall notice, and drops anything the model invented.

02:17.973 --> 02:22.267
B: Pick any provider: Bedrock, Anthropic, an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, or a local model.

02:22.267 --> 02:27.634
B: Patient names and birth dates stay out of the prompts, and every run is logged.

02:27.694 --> 02:29.151
A: Security is built in.

02:29.151 --> 02:34.977
A: PHI fields are encrypted, roles are enforced on the server, and the audit log is hash-chained.

02:34.977 --> 02:37.162
A: These are HIPAA-style safeguards, not certified.

02:37.222 --> 02:38.057
A: Built with Kiro.

02:38.057 --> 02:42.788
A: Specs carry requirement IDs, steering holds the safety rules, and hooks run a PHI guard on save.

02:42.788 --> 02:47.520
A: A custom agent and a Kiro Crew team did the work, with a human at every gate.

02:47.580 --> 02:48.489
A: Chimera Rx.

02:48.489 --> 02:50.306
A: github.com/pjborad/Chimera-Rx.

02:50.306 --> 02:52.124
A: pjborad.github.io/Chimera-Rx.

02:52.124 --> 02:53.487
A: Synthetic data only.
